{"resource":{"id":"react-pdf-notes","title":"React.js — PDF Notes","category":"Web Development","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"63 min","pages":128,"lastUpdated":"August 2026","tags":["Web Development","React","Hooks"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Chapter-wise React.js notes covering beginner to advanced concepts — components, JSX, state, props, hooks, Context, routing, forms, API, auth, performance, testing, deployment, and React 19."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"ch1","label":"Ch 1. Introduction"},{"id":"ch2","label":"Ch 2. JSX & Rendering"},{"id":"ch3","label":"Ch 3. Components & Props"},{"id":"ch4","label":"Ch 4. State & Events"},{"id":"ch5","label":"Ch 5. Hooks"},{"id":"ch6","label":"Ch 6. Context API"},{"id":"ch7","label":"Ch 7. Routing"},{"id":"ch8","label":"Ch 8. Forms"},{"id":"ch9","label":"Ch 9. API Integration"},{"id":"ch10","label":"Ch 10. Authentication"},{"id":"ch11","label":"Ch 11. Performance"},{"id":"ch12","label":"Ch 12. Testing"},{"id":"ch13","label":"Ch 13. Deployment"},{"id":"ch14","label":"Ch 14. React 19"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"React.js — Quick Revision Notes","tag":"Web Development","time":"10 min"},{"title":"React.js — Cheat Sheet","tag":"Web Development","time":"5 min"},{"title":"React.js — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Web Development","time":"44 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Full chapter-wise reference for React from setup to production.</li>\n          <li>Formatted for offline revision and exam prep.</li>\n          <li>Includes code snippets, comparison tables, and best practices per chapter.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 1 — Introduction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>React is a component-based UI library maintained by Meta. It uses a virtual DOM to update the UI efficiently and encourages declarative code.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — React ecosystem: core library, router, state manager, tooling.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 2 — JSX &amp; Rendering</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>const el = &lt;h1 class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Hello&lt;/h1&gt;;\n// compiles to\nReact.createElement(&quot;h1&quot;, { className: &quot;title&quot; }, &quot;Hello&quot;);</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 3 — Components &amp; Props</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Function components accept props and return JSX. Props are read-only.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>function Avatar({ src, alt }) { return &lt;img src={src} alt={alt} /&gt;; }</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 4 — State &amp; Events</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>const [count, setCount] = useState(0);\n&lt;button onClick={() =&gt; setCount(c =&gt; c + 1)}&gt;+&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 5 — Hooks</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Rules: call at top level only; call from React functions only. Core hooks: useState, useEffect, useRef, useMemo, useCallback, useReducer, useContext, useLayoutEffect, useTransition, useDeferredValue, useId.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 6 — Context API</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>const AuthCtx = createContext(null);\nconst useAuth = () =&gt; useContext(AuthCtx);</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 7 — Routing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>React Router v6+: declarative routes, nested layouts, outlet, loaders, actions.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 8 — Forms</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Controlled inputs bind value to state. Uncontrolled use refs. Prefer React Hook Form for large forms.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 9 — API Integration</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Use TanStack Query for server state. Never store server data in useState long-term.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 10 — Authentication</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Session via httpOnly cookie or short-lived JWT + refresh token. Route guards redirect unauthenticated users.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 11 — Performance</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Memoize expensive components with <code>React.memo</code>.</li>\n          <li>Split bundles with <code>React.lazy</code>.</li>\n          <li>Virtualize long lists.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Performance funnel: measure, memoize, split, virtualize.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 12 — Testing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Unit tests with Vitest + Testing Library. E2E with Playwright.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch13\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 13 — Deployment</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Build static assets, configure SPA fallback, add caching headers, deploy to CDN.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ch14\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Chapter 14 — React 19</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Actions, useOptimistic, useFormStatus, the <code>use()</code> hook, and Server Components for hybrid rendering.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>These notes cover the full React surface area needed to ship production apps. Revisit chapters as topics arise on the job.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Are class components still supported?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes, but new code should use function components + hooks.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is Redux dead?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No — Redux Toolkit is the modern approach and still widely used.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational notes. Verify APIs against the official React documentation.</p>\n      </div></section>"}